28,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems that a high upfront cost is a barrier for newcomers, and previous tiered systems caused friction among members.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The administrative side is a nightmare. Chasing small payments is incredibly time-consuming, and mid-year calculations are a tedious manual process.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,My findings confirm a significant imbalance. A small group handles almost all the attendance and the physical labor of the club.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,There is a clear correlation between charging for specific events and a drop in regular attendance. People are becoming hesitant.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Most of our costs are fixed—hall hire and insurance—regardless of turnout. Also, getting people to pay on time is a struggle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the costs are mostly fixed, we must ensure the base fee covers them without being so high that it scares off new members.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, if a few people do everything, a flat fee might feel unfair to them, but a complex system will kill the treasurer.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The current system is unfair to the regulars, but we must consider the effort required to manage a more ""fair"" one.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the ""hesitancy"" I found suggests that any move toward activity-based charging could further alienate our regulars.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, I don't care how many hours it takes if the alternative is the account running dry because we guessed the fee wrong.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We are balancing three things: accessibility for newcomers, fairness for the regulars, and the sanity of the treasurer.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, sanity is a resource too. If the treasurer quits every year, the account will be a mess regardless of the fee.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We need a system that acknowledges the regulars without creating a bureaucratic monster that discourages the casual members.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we make it too transactional, we lose the feeling of belonging. That is the most dangerous risk of all.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I just want a figure we can actually count on. We can't run a club on ""feelings of belonging"" if the insurance isn't paid.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
